  "key_evidence": [
    "Why it matters: Home Depot spent money in court to stop its own staff wearing union badges. The Eighth Circuit's November 2025 decision in Home Depot U.S.A., Inc. v. NLRB expanded the \"special circumstances\" exception letting employers restrict union insignia.",
    "A store organising drive cited a starting wage of about $14.50 - lower than the Walmart in the same shopping centre.",
    "The positive side is real and large: about $739 million in bonuses to non-management employees, 10 million training hours committed to frontline associates and 2.5 million to leaders by 2028, and the Homer Fund making hardship grants to associates since 1999. Action scores 3.20 of 5.",
    "Corrections do not stick. Home Depot paid a $1.7 million civil penalty in September 2024 for charging above advertised prices; a new consumer class action making the same complaint was filed in March 2026.",
    "NO IN-WINDOW EVIDENCE drove this movement. The scanner searched Home Depot individually and found none. This is a first measurement of a value that was never evidenced."
  ],
